    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situate on an elevated site in Moneen, Louisburgh, this detached bungalow presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a midway between Louisburgh town and the stunning Old Head Beach, the property enjoys the perfect balance of rural tranquillity and convenient access to local amenities, schools, shops, and some of Mayo's most spectacular coastal scenery.\r\nWhile the property would benefit from updating and modernisation, it offers well-proportioned accommodation throughout and provides an ideal canvas for purchasers seeking to create a comfortable family home, holiday retreat, or investment property in a prime location.\r\nAccommodation begins with a welcoming entrance hall leading to a bright and spacious sitting room positioned to the front of the property. A large picture window floods the room with natural light while capturing pleasant views of the surrounding countryside, and an open fireplace creates a warm focal point for family gatherings and relaxing evenings.\r\nThe kitchen and dining area forms the heart of the home, offering generous space for everyday living and entertaining. The fitted kitchen provides ample storage and workspace, while adjoining utility and laundry rooms add valuable practicality. A convenient guest WC is also located off the utility area.\r\nThere are three well-proportioned bedrooms, two enjoying attractive front-facing countryside views and a third positioned to the rear, providing a quiet and comfortable retreat. A fully tiled shower room completes the accommodation.\r\nSet on a peaceful site with ample off street parking, a large front garden and a detached garage, the property enjoys a highly desirable setting just minutes from both Louisburgh and the renowned Blue Flag beach at Old Head. The combination of its superb location, generous accommodation and potential for refurbishment makes this an exciting opportunity for buyers seeking a home in a truly exceptional part of the west of Ireland."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall:\t\t1.48m x 3.66m\r\nInner hall:\t\t6.90m x 5.18m\r\nSitting room:\t\t3.78m x 4.06m\r\nKitchen/dining room:\t6.13m x 3.40m\r\nUtility:\t\t\t2.94m x 3.63m\r\nLaundry:\t\t4.31m x 2.83m\r\nBedroom 1:\t\t3.52m x 3.64m\r\nBedroom 2:\t\t2.60m x 4.48m\r\nBedroom 3:\t\t3.41m x 3.74m\r\nShower room:\t\t3.44m x 1.70m\r\nApprox Internal Floor Area: \r\nc.112.20 sq.m (c.1,207.7 sq.ft)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "\tPrime residential setting between Louisburgh town & renowned Old Head Beach\r\n\t3-bed (one ensuite) bungalow residence extending to c.1,207 sq.ft\r\n\tAn ideal choice for a first-time buyer, retirement retreat, or holiday home\r\n\tConvenient access to schools, shops, beaches and outdoor amenities\r\n\tExcellent opportunity to refurbish and create a home to your own specification\r\n\tLocated on an elevated site with views of Sheeffry and Croagh Patrick"
